WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.880
- I think that the risk of the Democrats

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.550
is they fall as out of touch with people,

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.040
living in the Midwest,
living wherever else it is

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.340
in this country.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.270
Open-door immigration
got Brexit over the line

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.020
and has destroyed socialism
in the United Kingdom.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.680
And that I think is a
very inspiring message.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.450
But, it needs a Republican Party

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.630
that's got a distinct, clear message

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.300
as to how they're gonna
deal with the crisis.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.860
So they've got to get
themselves organized.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.748
But with the right message,

00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:31.030
there are an awful lot of Democrat voters

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.889
that will vote Republican next year.

00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:35.806
(slow tempo music)

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:40.740
- I'm Dave Rubin, and joining me today

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.900
is a British activist,
commentator, former leader

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.010
of the UK Independence Party,

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:49.100
as well as the former
leader of the Brexit Party.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.970
And now he's on tour
right here in the US of A,

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.170
Nigel Farage.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.860
I don't know how we
haven't done this before.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.030
Finally, welcome to the The Rubin Report.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.710
- Well, I'm delighted to be here,

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:04.500
and yeah, I've come actually
with a very optimistic message

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.650
because I know a lot of Conservatives here

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.990
are really down at the moment, you know,

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:11.680
down that their guy got 75 million votes

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:12.990
and somehow didn't win.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.890
Down about what's going on in our cities

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.570
with a deliberate attempt to
divide black and white people,

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:20.940
which is horrendous,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.110
and down about what Biden might do.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:25.927
Is he gonna pack the court, or
I mean, all of these things.

00:01:25.927 --> 00:01:28.450
And my sense from my American friends,

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.480
is some of them are down

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.290
to the point of being disillusioned.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.395
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:01:32.395 --> 00:01:34.510
- And disillusioned movements,

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:37.410
pessimistic movements don't win.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.290
So the message I've come with is this.

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:43.900
We voted Brexit June 23rd,
2016, a great historic night.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.400
Three years later, guess what?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.030
Our contract, our contract
to leave on March 29th, 2019,

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.860
we woke up on March 30th.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.820
Not only had we not left,

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.950
it looked like there was
no prospect of us leaving.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.770
And yet, we led a grassroots
rebellion fight back.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.510
We've smashed the establishment.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.470
We've won.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.040
We've got Brexit.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.410
The Socialist Party in the UK,

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.240
who were heavily on the remain side,

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.230
and heavily pro open borders,

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:16.000
are literally being crushed
electorally week by week.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.920
And my message is, however bad it looks,

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.570
actually this administration

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:21.910
are making some terrible mistakes.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.600
What is happening on the border,

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.750
effectively, turns every
state into a border state.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.430
So my message is, don't be down.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:32.040
Don't be mad.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.387
There's a big chance here for
a massive victory in 2022,

00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:38.060
and an even bigger one in 2024.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.320
But the right in America needs to unite,

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.290
needs to have some common messaging,

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.160
just one or two less egos around the place

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.620
might be quite helpful.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.453
But don't-

00:02:48.453 --> 00:02:51.960
Look, if we could beat
the global establishment

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.400
and get Brexit back over
the line, you can do it.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.760
- So I love the message, obviously.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.810
There's something kind of funny.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.290
You're coming to America
to bring less ego.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:04.310
That's a tough one, that's a tough one.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.190
But one of the things
that I love about you,

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.250
and we've gotten to know each other

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.310
over the years a little bit.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:11.170
We've had a couple of gin and
tonics together once or twice.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.003
- We sure have, yep.

00:03:12.003 --> 00:03:15.210
- But you're the type of
politician that actually does

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.110
instead of just talks.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.013
Can you talk a little bit
about what that is like?

00:03:19.013 --> 00:03:22.360
Because I think most people
see politicians at this point,

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.670
basically just as bureaucrats

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.320
who pretty much just take
their money and do nothing,

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.850
or maybe lock them in their homes.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.790
But you actually make things happen,

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.410
and that's gotta be very
different than most of the people

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:34.990
that you're around often,

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:37.470
or have been around over the years.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:42.470
- So in June '99, against the
flow, totally unpredicted,

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.690
I found myself being elected as a member

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:47.810
of the European parliament.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:48.700
And everybody was shocked.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:49.533
Yeah, who is this guy?

00:03:49.533 --> 00:03:51.310
What's this new party?

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.860
And I remember the next
morning, the phone rang,

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.780
and it was a guy who'd been a commentator

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:56.970
and a satirist in Britain,

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.800
a guy called Christopher
Booker, very intelligent man.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.657
And Christopher said to
me that morning, he said,

00:04:01.657 --> 00:04:04.467
"Nigel, after 40 years
of study, I can tell you,

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:07.247
"there are two types
of people in politics.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.487
"There are those who want to be someone,

00:04:09.487 --> 00:04:11.843
"and there are those who
want to do something.

00:04:11.843 --> 00:04:13.370
"And make your mind up young man."

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.400
I was young then.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.367
He said, "Make your mind up young man,

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.513
"which of those you want to be?"

00:04:18.513 --> 00:04:19.820
And here's the point.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.390
He was absolutely right.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.920
The vast majority of people
in politics are there

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:27.340
for rank, title, position, status.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:30.328
And they'll do, I mean,
they'll sell their grandmothers

00:04:30.328 --> 00:04:32.040
to climb the greasy pole,

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.170
because for them it's all
about career advancement.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.570
Then you get people in
politics who are doing it

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.720
out of genuine conviction

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:41.270
because they believe the
agenda they're pursuing

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.830
is gonna make their country better,

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.056
and the lives of their people better.

00:04:45.056 --> 00:04:49.000
And I personally couldn't
give a damn about titles.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.987
People say, "oh, you know,
you're not Lord Nigel,

00:04:50.987 --> 00:04:52.060
"you're not Sir Nigel."

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.590
I couldn't care less about any of that.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.870
I did this because I could
see globalism building.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:01.260
Back in the 1990s, I could see bureaucracy

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.120
was beginning to win over democracy,

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.530
and I was determined to
do something about it.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:09.140
So yeah, I'm a doer, and
I'm not here for the fight.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.430
- Do you remember when you first saw it?

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:14.010
When was the first moment
that you saw something

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.373
that really alarmed you?

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.640
- The first big moment was in 1990

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:24.420
when the government pegged Sterling

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.480
against the basket of European currencies.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:27.930
Effectively, the Deutsche Mark.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.720
Now, you know, anybody with
any economic history knows

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.810
all pegged currency
systems end in disaster.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.640
None of them through time ever succeed.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.170
And they'd done it because
they wanted us to join

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.460
what became the Euro.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.800
And that was the first alarm bell,

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.460
that whatever they were
telling the electorate,

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.000
come general election time,

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.720
actually, they were literally
selling off our country.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.910
And then there was a rebellion.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.400
In 1993, there was a rebellion.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:58.430
Backbench Conservatives rebelled
over a new European treaty.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:02.250
The treaty that turned it
from an European community

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.149
into a European union
with a flag, and anthem,

00:06:05.149 --> 00:06:05.982
and all of those things.

00:06:05.982 --> 00:06:07.940
And I watched this rebellion.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:09.700
And right at the last minute, John Major,

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.060
who was the Prime Minister,

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.360
used a motion of confidence

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:15.257
to get this treaty pushed through.

00:06:15.257 --> 00:06:16.820
And I couldn't believe it.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:17.653
Well, hang on.

00:06:17.653 --> 00:06:19.230
You've been telling me guys

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:22.600
that if this treaty goes through,
we lose our independence.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.710
And yet when it came to it,
you decided to put your career,

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.740
you decided to put your party

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.300
above the interests of the country.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:34.190
And I realized then that the
so-called Tory Euroskeptics

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:38.510
were frankly a bunch of chinless
wonders, a bunch of losers.

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:40.850
None of them have a stomach for the fight.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:44.277
And I said in '93, "I'm gonna do this.

00:06:44.277 --> 00:06:46.717
"I don't care if people laugh at me.

00:06:46.717 --> 00:06:49.357
"I don't care if I'm the only
person that votes for me.

00:06:49.357 --> 00:06:52.390
"I'm gonna fight this and do
this as a matter of principle."

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.658
And you know, frankly,

00:06:54.658 --> 00:06:58.690
that moment that spelt the
next 27 years of my life.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:01.450
- Did you have any idea the opposition

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:02.700
that you were gonna come against?

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.730
I mean, when I was in London last time,

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.550
when I saw you it was during
the tour with Jordan Peterson,

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:08.710
and it was in the middle of Brexit,

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.010
but there was still a huge feeling like,

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:12.770
ah, maybe it's not gonna happen,

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:15.070
and maybe the bureaucrats
still will take over

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:16.540
or do some last minute tricks.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.240
And then of course it was framed

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.530
that all the people that
supported it were racists,

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:22.090
and bigots, and all the rest of it.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:25.490
But just the endless
machine that we now all see

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:27.190
that has been so exposed.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:29.070
And in many ways, from
an American perspective,

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:31.280
thanks to Donald Trump was so exposed.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:34.990
Did you realize how crazy
that machine was gonna be,

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:37.713
and what it was gonna do
to you and your supporters?

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.960
- Gandhi, of course, fought
the campaign for India

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.410
to leave the British empire
and to get his independence.

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:47.757
And Gandhi once said,
"First they ignore you.

00:07:47.757 --> 00:07:49.327
"Then they laugh at you.

00:07:49.327 --> 00:07:50.313
"Then they attack you.

00:07:50.313 --> 00:07:51.500
"And then you win."

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:54.900
And I went through every
one of those four stages.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:58.620
You know, in the beginning I
was being ignored completely.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.456
When they couldn't ignore me,

00:08:00.456 --> 00:08:02.180
I think I was the most cartooned,

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.020
the most lampooned person on comedy shows.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.610
It was as if, I was like
the sort of patron saint

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.110
of lost causes.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:12.840
And then, and then the
moment that it really changed

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:17.060
was in 2004, eight, and then
10 former communist countries

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.600
joined the European Union

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.400
with total rights of free movement.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.580
And this led to millions of people

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.780
coming into the United Kingdom.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:27.100
It was too much, too quickly.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.400
It was out of control.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.800
And that was the moment when
I linked the immigration issue

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.470
with the sovereignty issue,
the independence issue.

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:37.710
And that was the moment that
the establishment turned on me,

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:41.010
and they spent basically the next 15 years

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:43.300
trying to tell anyone that would listen,

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:47.160
that I was a racist leading
a dark dangerous movement

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.370
that harked back to the 1930s.

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:51.520
I mean, nothing could have been, David,

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:54.910
nothing could have been
further from the truth.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:56.230
That is what they tried to do.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:59.050
And I have to tell you, in all honesty,

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:03.480
if I had known just how
horrible my life was gonna be,

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.760
I don't know whether I would have done it.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:06.737
I mean, you know, I finished up

00:09:06.737 --> 00:09:10.800
having to live with
protection round the clock.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.277
If you went out somewhere,
people threw things at you.

00:09:13.277 --> 00:09:16.240
And this was the media,
this was mainstream media

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.810
working with big global corporations

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:22.040
trying to maintain
their own self-interest.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.150
But in the end, in the end, you know,

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:27.860
you can keep pushing
accusations against somebody,

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.610
but if you can't prove it,

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:31.590
it's a little bit like crying wolf.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.350
And in the end, people saw through it.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:36.570
But yeah, it was tough, it was hard.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:39.720
And then, you know, I was
perhaps guilty of some naivety.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.030
Because on the 23rd of June, 2016,

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.410
that moment where we've won,

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.170
and all the parties promised

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.970
that they would honor the result.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:50.400
And then we saw a three-year campaign.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.280
As you say, we were told we
didn't know what we voted for.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.210
We were told property
prices would collapse.

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:59.740
We were told millions
of jobs would be lost.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.890
We were told foreign direct investment

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:04.100
from America and elsewhere would dry up.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:08.360
We were even told, brace
yourself for this one,

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:11.070
we even told there would be an outbreak

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:13.940
of super gonorrhea in the country

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:15.880
because the drug that was used to treat it

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:16.840
came from Germany,

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:19.230
and we wouldn't even
get supplies of drugs.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:22.680
I mean, there is no depth

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.790
to which these people did not sing.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.100
But the resolve of the British people

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.290
did not budge one inch.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:33.120
And I believe there is a parallel.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:35.640
I don't believe those 75 million people

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.810
who voted for Donald Trump
have changed their mind.

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:40.930
If I think in many ways,
probably in their hearts

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:43.590
they feel it even more strongly.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:46.147
And that's why I'm on this
tour, to spread that message,

00:10:46.147 --> 00:10:49.450
a message of optimism, a message
that you can beat the odds,

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:50.283
you really can.

00:10:50.283 --> 00:10:51.116
- I know you're a pro,

00:10:51.116 --> 00:10:53.470
because you just did the exact
transition I was going for,

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.240
because there are so many parallels

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.480
to what's happening in America right now.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.160
And everything that you just described

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.860
that the UK has been going
through for, you know,

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.480
really the last 20 years.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:06.150
Are you sort of surprised that America,

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.330
that Conservatives, or
right-leaning people,

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.020
or anyone that cares about that flag

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.230
that's right behind you,

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.700
that everyone seems a
little bit lost right now,

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.920
that there really is a
shell shock situation since,

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.420
really, I think it started
probably on January 6th,

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:20.950
but then once Biden took over,

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.520
and that he's been so
much further to the left

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:25.650
than most people thought.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:28.080
Not that I thought, but that, you know,

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.423
the pundit class thought.

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:32.420
- Yeah look, I think, yeah,

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:35.820
obviously the election result was a shock.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:39.070
The events of January
the 6th were unsavory.

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:40.920
There's no other way of putting it.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:41.850
And it's been difficult.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.520
It's been very, very difficult.

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:47.140
And yes, as you say, Biden
being pulled to the left,

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:50.560
Biden, you know, even
dropping references to God,

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:51.393
which I think shocked--

00:11:51.393 --> 00:11:52.310
- Just this morning, yeah.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.150
- Many, many, yeah, yeah.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.930
Many, many tens of millions of Americans.

00:11:56.930 --> 00:12:00.060
I understand why people
feel depressed and down.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:05.060
But look, I was getting this
in 2018 in the UK, into 2019.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:08.227
Everyone saying to me, "Nigel,
it's done, it's finished,

00:12:08.227 --> 00:12:09.170
"it's not gonna happen."

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:11.530
And I kept saying to them, "No".

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.340
And I spent that period of time planning,

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:17.520
planning the next fight back,
planning my next big campaign,

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.680
because I knew, I just knew

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:22.580
