00:18:06.555 --> 00:18:10.270
You know, it was a working class movement.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:14.010
It was quite strongly Methodist
as well, sort of low church.

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:17.160
High church for the Tories,
low church for Labor

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:18.220
was kind of how it was.

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:22.360
And it was genuinely a
working class movement.

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:26.230
But a patriotic working class movement.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:28.270
The Labor Party, you know,

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:31.470
whatever socialist policies
they brought in post 1945,

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:33.210
they believed in the country.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.130
You know, Clement Attlee
who was the Prime Minister

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:36.810
that brought in the welfare state,

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:39.640
on his door, it said
"Major Clement Attlee."

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:43.690
He was proud of the first World
War service that he'd given.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:45.940
And what has happened to the Labor Party,

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:50.490
is it's become a party of the
globalist metropolitan elite.

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:53.020
It's become a party predominantly

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.740
