And for them, of course,
the right thing, you know,

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:54.510
the kick they get is they
feel morally superior.

00:22:54.510 --> 00:22:57.430
They actually think they're
better people than we are.

00:22:57.430 --> 00:23:00.200
But none of that works when you go out

00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:03.770
to a good ordinary decent
folk who work hard,

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:05.990
bring up their families, and you know,

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:07.300
Reagan was very good at this,

00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:10.930
very good at getting
Democrats to vote Republican.

00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:12.377
Trump has been very good.

00:23:12.377 --> 00:23:14.610
And there is a kind of
a realignment I think,

00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:16.647
going on within American politics.

00:23:16.647 --> 00:23:21.010
And I think the opportunity
that it provides for 2022

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:22.240
is simply enormous.

00:23:22.240 --> 00:23:23.543
- Where do you think Trump fits into that

00:23:23.543 --> 00:23:25.790
because that seems to be
the outlier at the moment.

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:27.070
It's like, is he gonna run?

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:29.020
Does he, you know, what I've
been trying to tell people,

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:30.970
is to me, it seems like
the best thing he could do

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:34.270
is basically be the
outsider taking the fire.

00:23:34.270 --> 00:23:36.020
And then you get a guy like DeSantis

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:37.730
to just run right through.

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:39.120
That seems to make sense to me.

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:41.340
But you know, Trump
obviously does whatever

00:23:41.340 --> 00:23:42.693
Trump thinks is best.

00:23:44.070 --> 00:23:47.050
- Yeah, I have spent some
time with him on this trip,

00:23:47.050 --> 00:23:49.500
and that's a meeting of friends basically.

00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:50.913
And we have become friends.

00:23:52.010 --> 00:23:55.570
I said, this is what I said to him, okay?

00:23:55.570 --> 00:23:57.267
And you know, I won't say what he said,

00:23:57.267 --> 00:23:59.360
but this is what I said to him.

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:02.167
I said, "Look, we've
got the external threat

00:24:02.167 --> 00:24:04.457
"of the Chinese Communist Party

00:24:04.457 --> 00:24:05.970
"getting more and more aggressive."

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:09.740
And who's to say in Taiwan
or elsewhere what might occur

00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:12.460
over the course of the next few years.

00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:14.090
We've got the internal threat,

00:24:14.090 --> 00:24:15.860
which of course is cancel culture

00:24:15.860 --> 00:24:17.100
and the threats that represents

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:19.380
the free speech and everything else.

00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:23.007
And I said to him, "I don't see anybody

00:24:23.007 --> 00:24:27.207
"who's got the courage or the charisma

00:24:27.207 --> 00:24:29.127
"to fight those things."

00:24:29.127 --> 00:24:31.877
"Now, if somebody else comes along,

00:24:31.877 --> 00:24:35.297
"who's got the big charisma
that can do the job,

00:24:35.297 --> 00:24:38.577
"that can rally people in
those working class communities

00:24:38.577 --> 00:24:42.507
"to go out and maybe for the
first time, vote Republican,

00:24:42.507 --> 00:24:45.060
"if that person comes along then fine."

00:24:45.060 --> 00:24:46.410
But you know something?

00:24:46.410 --> 00:24:50.270
Donald Trump, people like him
don't come along very often.

00:24:50.270 --> 00:24:54.827
I mean, the guy has got an
incredible animal magnetism,

00:24:54.827 --> 00:24:57.720
and he's shown more courage as a leader

00:24:57.720 --> 00:25:01.010
than any global leader
I've seen in my lifetime.

00:25:01.010 --> 00:25:04.770
That guy was under relentless
assault from day one,

00:25:04.770 --> 00:25:06.770
just as they tried to stop Brexit,

00:25:06.770 --> 00:25:08.480
they tried to de-legitimized him.

00:25:08.480 --> 00:25:10.270
You know, and it never stopped.

00:25:10.270 --> 00:25:13.110
And of course, even if
eased back on his policies,

00:25:13.110 --> 00:25:15.630
they would have eased back on
the pressure, but he didn't.

00:25:15.630 --> 00:25:17.010
He's got the courage of a lion.

00:25:17.010 --> 00:25:19.080
Now look, he's got his faults.

00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:19.990
Of course he has.

00:25:19.990 --> 00:25:22.140
We've all got our faults.

00:25:22.140 --> 00:25:26.540
But you know, in his heart,
and with his instincts,

00:25:26.540 --> 00:25:28.010
does he stand for the right things?

00:25:28.010 --> 00:25:29.330
I truly believe that he does.

00:25:29.330 --> 00:25:32.059
So you know, let's see
what happens, you know,

00:25:32.059 --> 00:25:35.160
as the next couple of years roll out.

00:25:35.160 --> 00:25:37.010
But you know what?

00:25:37.010 --> 00:25:40.040
When I saw him, he's lost a lot of weight.

00:25:40.040 --> 00:25:43.300
He's playing loads of golf,
taking loads of exercise.

00:25:43.300 --> 00:25:46.010
He looks younger than he looked in 2016.

00:25:46.010 --> 00:25:48.494
I mean, most American Presidents age.

00:25:48.494 --> 00:25:53.010
Obama and co, we'll see them
graying before your eyes.

00:25:53.010 --> 00:25:55.780
And the fact that he's gonna
be 78 next time around,

00:25:55.780 --> 00:25:56.613
well, who knows.

00:25:56.613 --> 00:25:59.870
But God willing, if he's
in the same kind of shape

00:25:59.870 --> 00:26:00.850
that he's in now,

00:26:00.850 --> 00:26:02.530
there's nothing to stop him from doing it.

00:26:02.530 --> 00:26:06.080
And the other point here
that's worth mentioning,

00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:09.040
I went to, I think it
was eight of the rallies

00:26:09.040 --> 00:26:12.860
and the run-up to the November
election all over America.

00:26:12.860 --> 00:26:14.270
I want to tell you something.

00:26:14.270 --> 00:26:15.490
I've never seen enthusiasm.

00:26:15.490 --> 00:26:16.460
- No, I know, I know.

00:26:16.460 --> 00:26:19.930
- I've never ever seen anything like it.

00:26:19.930 --> 00:26:22.957
They admire this man, they love this man.

00:26:22.957 --> 00:26:26.173
And I would say to, you know,

00:26:26.173 --> 00:26:30.370
those in a position of
power within the party,

00:26:30.370 --> 00:26:33.940
if you really think you can
find someone better than this,

00:26:33.940 --> 00:26:34.773
well, good luck to you.

00:26:34.773 --> 00:26:35.606
- You know, it's kind of funny

00:26:35.606 --> 00:26:39.130
because I remember when I met
you for breakfast one morning

00:26:39.130 --> 00:26:41.020
and we took a picture
and I posted the picture,

00:26:41.020 --> 00:26:42.177
and then people were saying,

00:26:42.177 --> 00:26:43.637
"Oh look, you're with that racist.

00:26:43.637 --> 00:26:44.530
"That racist."

00:26:44.530 --> 00:26:46.490
And meanwhile, we sat there for two hours,

00:26:46.490 --> 00:26:47.450
we talked about freedom,

00:26:47.450 --> 00:26:48.920
we talk about liberty, all this stuff.

00:26:48.920 --> 00:26:51.510
And it's very similar to
going to a Trump rally

00:26:51.510 --> 00:26:53.827
when I started going to those
rallies, and I'm thinking,

00:26:53.827 --> 00:26:55.557
"Oh, am I going to see these racists here

00:26:55.557 --> 00:26:56.710
"or something like that?"

00:26:56.710 --> 00:27:00.020
And it's the happiest, most joyful people,

00:27:00.020 --> 00:27:02.760
who in many cases are
not political at all.

00:27:02.760 --> 00:27:05.310
They're just there because
they want to express

00:27:05.310 --> 00:27:06.480
some level of freedom.

00:27:06.480 --> 00:27:07.480
Something like that.

00:27:08.530 --> 00:27:09.560
- Yeah no, absolutely.

00:27:09.560 --> 00:27:12.620
I mean, this has been a
constant attempt for the left

00:27:12.620 --> 00:27:14.840
to tarnish us with this racism word,

00:27:14.840 --> 00:27:16.600
and it just doesn't work anymore.

00:27:16.600 --> 00:27:19.500
The real racists are actually those

00:27:19.500 --> 00:27:20.420
behind Black Lives Matter.

00:27:20.420 --> 00:27:21.577
I really mean that.

00:27:21.577 --> 00:27:23.160
And I really mean that.

00:27:23.160 --> 00:27:26.120
You know, when Martin Luther King said

00:27:26.120 --> 00:27:27.117
in that amazing speech,

00:27:27.117 --> 00:27:30.110
and I mean, what an orator the guy was.

00:27:30.110 --> 00:27:34.587
But when he said, "I want my
four children to be judged,

00:27:34.587 --> 00:27:37.037
"not for the color of their skin,

00:27:37.037 --> 00:27:39.830
"but by the content of their character."

00:27:39.830 --> 00:27:43.140
And now what's happening
through BLM and elsewhere,

00:27:43.140 --> 00:27:46.640
is we are dividing people
up into different groups,

00:27:46.640 --> 00:27:51.010
dividing them up on the grounds
of race, ethnicity, gender,

00:27:51.010 --> 00:27:52.227
whatever else it may be.

00:27:52.227 --> 00:27:54.350
And that is disastrous.

00:27:54.350 --> 00:27:55.990
That is destructive.

00:27:55.990 --> 00:27:57.490
That is the real racism.

00:27:57.490 --> 00:27:59.250
And I loathe it.

00:27:59.250 --> 00:28:03.900
I wanna live in a country where everybody

00:28:03.900 --> 00:28:07.230
is treated exactly the same.

00:28:07.230 --> 00:28:09.440
'Cause if you start
giving special privileges

00:28:09.440 --> 00:28:10.700
to certain groups,

00:28:10.700 --> 00:28:13.440
you then automatically
alienate other groups,

00:28:13.440 --> 00:28:14.880
who feel left out.

00:28:14.880 --> 00:28:19.500
A free, fair society would
have equality of opportunity

00:28:19.500 --> 00:28:20.333
for all.

00:28:20.333 --> 00:28:24.420
And of course, I condemn
and loathe racism.

00:28:24.420 --> 00:28:25.750
And yes, there are some,

00:28:25.750 --> 00:28:28.150
there is a fringe on the extreme right,

00:28:28.150 --> 00:28:29.270
who I think we should simply,

00:28:29.270 --> 00:28:32.180
they would have nothing
to do with whatsoever.

00:28:32.180 --> 00:28:33.370
But you're quite right.

00:28:33.370 --> 00:28:35.250
You know, whether it
was my UKIP supporters,

00:28:35.250 --> 00:28:38.270
my Brexit Party supporters,
Trump supporters at the rallies,

00:28:38.270 --> 00:28:41.637
these are very, very good decent people.

00:28:41.637 --> 00:28:45.940
And the more mainstream
media, or Hillary Clinton

00:28:45.940 --> 00:28:47.700
pointing fingers at them and call them

00:28:47.700 --> 00:28:50.040
deplorable, or ignorant, or stupid,

00:28:50.040 --> 00:28:52.340
the greater their resolve to fight back.

00:28:52.340 --> 00:28:55.490
- What do you make about
how the BLM movement,

00:28:55.490 --> 00:28:58.960
some of the Antifa stuff that,
now that is being exported.

00:28:58.960 --> 00:29:00.530
I mean, you guys are seeing some of that

00:29:00.530 --> 00:29:01.940
on the streets of London now,

00:29:01.940 --> 00:29:05.199
and it's happening in other
Western countries as well.

00:29:05.199 --> 00:29:07.180
- You know, mean within 24 hours

00:29:07.180 --> 00:29:08.230
of the death of George Floyd,

00:29:08.230 --> 00:29:12.260
within 24 hours, there were
riots in the streets of London.

00:29:12.260 --> 00:29:15.690
So don't tell me this was
a spontaneous outpouring.

00:29:15.690 --> 00:29:17.260
This was all planned.

00:29:17.260 --> 00:29:19.440
They'd been waiting for the opportunity.

00:29:19.440 --> 00:29:21.000
And I was disgusted.

00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:23.820
I mean, to see the Cenotaph in London,

00:29:23.820 --> 00:29:27.190
the monument to one
and a half million dead

00:29:27.190 --> 00:29:29.900
fighting for liberty in two World Wars,

00:29:29.900 --> 00:29:31.620
to see that desecrated.

00:29:31.620 --> 00:29:35.167
To see the Churchill statue
repeatedly desecrated.

00:29:35.167 --> 00:29:40.030
And what stunned me was to
see British police officers

00:29:40.030 --> 00:29:42.360
taking the knee in the streets.

00:29:42.360 --> 00:29:43.457
- And your police officers,

00:29:43.457 --> 00:29:45.557
your police officers don't even have guns.

00:29:46.540 --> 00:29:48.360
- They don't, well, some do, some do.

00:29:48.360 --> 00:29:50.430
Some do, but I think we're gonna have to,

00:29:50.430 --> 00:29:51.940
that's a policy that will need to change,

00:29:51.940 --> 00:29:53.415
no question about that.

00:29:53.415 --> 00:29:55.770
But to take the knee,

00:29:55.770 --> 00:29:59.290
and I was going on UK TV,
and radio, and writing,

00:29:59.290 --> 00:30:02.120
saying to everybody,
"Understand what this is."

00:30:02.120 --> 00:30:06.370
If this organization was
genuinely about equality,

00:30:06.370 --> 00:30:09.390
genuinely about getting
rid of racial prejudice,

00:30:09.390 --> 00:30:11.880
I'd have no problem with it whatsoever.

00:30:11.880 --> 00:30:13.360
But the truth of it is,

00:30:13.360 --> 00:30:15.951
and you've only gotta read their website.

00:30:15.951 --> 00:30:20.290
They tell you, they're in a
validly Marxist organization,

00:30:20.290 --> 00:30:22.490
intent on defunding the police,

00:30:22.490 --> 00:30:24.290
bringing down Western capitalism,

00:30:24.290 --> 00:30:28.160
and renew Marxist order to take its place.

00:30:28.160 --> 00:30:29.160
That is what they're doing.

00:30:29.160 --> 00:30:31.030
They are trying to destroy us.

00:30:31.030 --> 00:30:34.890
And yet I've been horrified
on both sides of the pond

00:30:34.890 --> 00:30:37.690
to see big corporations,

00:30:37.690 --> 00:30:40.080
you know, trying to say
wonderful things about them.

00:30:40.080 --> 00:30:44.790
I even saw St John's Church
opposite the White House.

00:30:44.790 --> 00:30:46.350
I was there yesterday.

00:30:46.350 --> 00:30:48.780
And they've got a Black
Lives Matter poster.

00:30:48.780 --> 00:30:50.090
What is going on?

00:30:50.090 --> 00:30:54.100
Don't people realize this is
a bad, dangerous organization?

00:30:54.100 --> 00:30:56.760
So you know, these are
things that really grieve me,

00:30:56.760 --> 00:31:00.670
and it's the lack of courage
of enough people to stand up

00:31:00.670 --> 00:31:03.740
and tell the truth for fear
of being called racist.

00:31:03.740 --> 00:31:04.750
- So with that all in mind,

00:31:04.750 --> 00:31:07.350
what do you think's gonna
happen with this mayoral race

00:31:07.350 --> 00:31:08.810
in London?

00:31:08.810 --> 00:31:11.713
'Cause it looks a little
messy at the moment.

00:31:13.010 --> 00:31:17.700
- Well, one of the things
that has changed politics

00:31:17.700 --> 00:31:21.240
in the United Kingdom
has been postal voting,

00:31:21.240 --> 00:31:22.550
early mail-out voting.

00:31:22.550 --> 00:31:26.310
We've seen it abused again,
and again, and again.

00:31:26.310 --> 00:31:28.580
There is no country in which this is safe.

00:31:28.580 --> 00:31:31.733
And I was trying to warn
America this time last year

00:31:31.733 --> 00:31:33.600
that if you went down this route,

00:31:33.600 --> 00:31:35.170
you know, the left will
always win at this.

00:31:35.170 --> 00:31:38.670
'Cause you see, if you think
you're morally superior,

00:31:38.670 --> 00:31:40.950
cheating is quite an easy thing to do.

00:31:40.950 --> 00:31:44.080
Whereas our side, just,
our side won't cheat.

00:31:44.080 --> 00:31:46.320
And I'm pleased to say that really,

00:31:46.320 --> 00:31:48.450
but you're never gonna win.

00:31:48.450 --> 00:31:52.200
The one country that's
got this right is France.

00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:54.480
Now the French, the French
don't get much right

00:31:54.480 --> 00:31:55.552
in my opinion,

00:31:55.552 --> 00:31:58.050
but the one thing they've got right,

00:31:58.050 --> 00:32:01.930
they've seen how open
postal voting is to fraud,

00:32:01.930 --> 00:32:05.440
intimidation, and abuse, and
they've banned it completely.

00:32:05.440 --> 00:32:06.780
So do you know what they do in France?

00:32:06.780 --> 00:32:09.340
If you wanna vote in France,
I'll tell you what happens.

00:32:09.340 --> 00:32:11.850
You go along to the local hall,

00:32:11.850 --> 00:32:14.340
you show your identification,

00:32:14.340 --> 00:32:16.140
you're given a piece of paper,

00:32:16.140 --> 00:32:19.410
you go into a polling booth in secrecy,

00:32:19.410 --> 00:32:23.810
you put a cross next to the
candidate or party you prefer.

00:32:23.810 --> 00:32:26.910
And after that, there are
no voting machines used.

00:32:26.910 --> 00:32:28.220
There's no need for those.

00:32:28.220 --> 00:32:29.640
They're manually counted.

00:32:29.640 --> 00:32:31.630
They're put in piles and totaled up.

00:32:31.630 --> 00:32:33.800
And that is free and open democracy.

00:32:33.800 --> 00:32:35.290
There's a big lesson we can learn from it.

00:32:35.290 --> 00:32:38.250
Now what Carter's has got
going for him in London,

00:32:38.250 --> 00:32:42.800
is they've signed up vast
numbers of the Muslim population

00:32:42.800 --> 00:32:44.170
to these postal votes.

00:32:44.170 --> 00:32:48.570
And I, look, I know that
in those communities,

00:32:48.570 --> 00:32:50.560
you know, the women are
signed up for postal votes,

00:32:50.560 --> 00:32:51.530
but do you actually think

00:32:51.530 --> 00:32:55.370
they ever, ever, ever get
the chance to exercise that?

00:32:55.370 --> 00:32:56.730
Of course they don't.

00:32:56.730 --> 00:33:01.630
I once saw, I once saw a box,

00:33:01.630 --> 00:33:05.830
a vote box being emptied
onto a table at a count

00:33:05.830 --> 00:33:08.740
in a place called Oldham
in the North of England.

00:33:08.740 --> 00:33:12.530
And unbelievably, of the
thousand or so ballots

00:33:12.530 --> 00:33:14.090
that were in that box,

00:33:14.090 --> 00:33:17.173
the percentage that were
voting for Labor was 100.

00:33:20.150 --> 00:33:22.210
That is literally impossible.

00:33:22.210 --> 00:33:25.470
So you know, that is
what keeping Sadiq Khan

00:33:25.470 --> 00:33:28.443
holding on in London is the
power of that postal vote.

00:33:29.390 --> 00:33:30.570
But even in London,

00:33:30.570 --> 00:33:33.110
which has been the great Labor stronghold,

00:33:33.110 --> 00:33:36.900
even there, the party is now seriously--

00:33:36.900 --> 00:33:38.640
- What do you think of
my friend Lawrence Fox?

00:33:38.640 --> 00:33:40.500
Do you think he has a chance to actually,

00:33:40.500 --> 00:33:43.320
from a liberal, a true
liberal perspective,

00:33:43.320 --> 00:33:45.170
do you think he has a chance to fight off

00:33:45.170 --> 00:33:48.160
the progressive movement onslaught?

00:33:48.160 --> 00:33:52.390
- Look, I admire
Lawrence, I like Lawrence.

00:33:52.390 --> 00:33:54.350
I mean, you know, he's a great guy.

00:33:54.350 --> 00:33:56.330
And the next time you're in
London, we'll go out together.

00:33:56.330 --> 00:33:58.323
You know, he is a great guy to be with.

00:34:00.360 --> 00:34:04.173
Starting new political
movements from scratch.

00:34:05.180 --> 00:34:06.707
- You know a little something about this.

00:34:06.707 --> 00:34:09.410
- I mean, it's done, you know,

00:34:09.410 --> 00:34:13.037
it took me so many years
to get UKIP set up.

00:34:13.037 --> 00:34:16.630
And in the end, we had 400
chapters around the country,

00:34:16.630 --> 00:34:19.700
millions of supporters, but
it doesn't happen overnight.

00:34:19.700 --> 00:34:22.450
Now the things that
Lawrence is battling for

00:34:22.450 --> 00:34:24.060
are fundamentally important issues.

00:34:24.060 --> 00:34:26.170
You know, it is about the relationship

00:34:26.170 --> 00:34:28.500
between the individual and the state.

00:34:28.500 --> 00:34:30.707
And this is something that we've
always prided ourselves on.

00:34:30.707 --> 00:34:33.550
You know, frankly ever since Magna Casa.

00:34:33.550 --> 00:34:35.730
But going all through the years,

00:34:35.730 --> 00:34:38.590
we've been the freest of
all European countries.

00:34:38.590 --> 00:34:40.890
In fact, the freest of all
the English speaking world.

00:34:40.890 --> 00:34:44.280
We've never had to have ID
cards, or any of these things.

00:34:44.280 --> 00:34:47.490
Now with COVID, we've seen
those liberties stripped away

00:34:47.490 --> 00:34:50.940
in the most remarkable
and very hasty fashion.

00:34:50.940 --> 00:34:54.060
So look, Lawrence, in terms
of making the arguments,

00:34:54.060 --> 00:34:55.710
he's in the right place.

00:34:55.710 --> 00:34:56.587
I wish him well.

00:34:56.587 --> 00:34:58.340
But if I'm being honest with you,

00:34:58.340 --> 00:35:00.307
it's gonna take a lot of
years to build a movement

00:35:00.307 --> 00:35:01.610
that's big enough to--

00:35:01.610 --> 00:35:03.260
- Do you make a distinction at this point

00:35:03.260 --> 00:35:04.640
between someone that would say

00:35:04.640 --> 00:35:07.070
they're an old school
liberal and a conservative.

00:35:07.070 --> 00:35:09.790
Does that even, is there any
distinction worth mentioning

00:35:09.790 --> 00:35:11.050
at this point?

00:35:11.050 --> 00:35:12.737
- Well I mean, it's a
funny thing, isn't it?

00:35:12.737 --> 00:35:15.947
You know, I mean, if you'd
said to me 20 years ago,

00:35:15.947 --> 00:35:18.990
"Nigel, where are you on
the left-right spectrum?"

00:35:18.990 --> 00:35:21.250
I'd have called myself
a Gladstonian liberal.

00:35:21.250 --> 00:35:23.740
You know, Gladstone was
a liberal Prime Minister

00:35:23.740 --> 00:35:26.170
back in the back of the 19th century,

00:35:26.170 --> 00:35:28.810
but one who believed in
freedom of the individual,

00:35:28.810 --> 00:35:31.250
you know, believed in the country.

00:35:31.250 --> 00:35:34.420
- A JFK Democrat from our
perspective, basically.

00:35:34.420 --> 00:35:35.320
- Yeah, yeah.

00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:38.271
I have to say, I've
stopped using the word.

00:35:38.271 --> 00:35:39.104
- Yeah, I get it.

00:35:39.104 --> 00:35:41.090
- You know, classical liberalism.

00:35:41.090 --> 00:35:44.150
You know, if you go to the Oxford Union,

00:35:44.150 --> 00:35:46.059
you know, and debate with
some of the brightest students

00:35:46.059 --> 00:35:47.250
in the world,

00:35:47.250 --> 00:35:49.750
maybe there, you can talk
about classical liberalism.

00:35:49.750 --> 00:35:51.350
If you try and talk about
classical liberalism

00:35:51.350 --> 00:35:52.960
to anybody else, they sort of,

00:35:52.960 --> 00:35:55.020
if they're Conservatives just go blah,

00:35:55.020 --> 00:36:00.020
because the word "liberal",
now means illiberal.

00:36:01.400 --> 00:36:03.610
The liberals wanna ban everything,

00:36:03.610 --> 00:36:05.770
the liberals wanna control everything.

00:36:05.770 --> 00:36:08.160
The liberals don't even
believe in free speech.

00:36:08.160 --> 00:36:10.590
So yeah, classical liberalism I'm afraid

00:36:10.590 --> 00:36:11.950
is only for the debating changes.

00:36:11.950 --> 00:36:13.850
- I get it, I wrote a book defending it,

00:36:13.850 --> 00:36:16.170
but I hear ya, I hear ya.

00:36:16.170 --> 00:36:18.620
You mentioned the lockdowns.

00:36:18.620 --> 00:36:20.060
You've had some difference of opinion

00:36:20.060 --> 00:36:21.300
with Boris Johnson on this.

00:36:21.300 --> 00:36:23.560
Where are you guys at
with lockdowns right now?

00:36:23.560 --> 00:36:27.393
Is it vastly different in the
cities versus the suburbs?

00:36:28.880 --> 00:36:31.410
- Well, the truth of it is,

00:36:31.410 --> 00:36:35.040
that Boris Johnson's
government were painfully slow

00:36:35.040 --> 00:36:36.867
to address the issue
when it first came to us.

00:36:36.867 --> 00:36:40.960
You know, 18 million people
flew into the United Kingdom

00:36:40.960 --> 00:36:43.520
during the first months of COVID-19

00:36:43.520 --> 00:36:46.423
without a single person even
being asked to take a test.

00:36:47.470 --> 00:36:50.540
You know, so we directly imported this.

00:36:50.540 --> 00:36:53.060
When the government then did decide

00:36:53.060 --> 00:36:55.910
it was gonna do something,
and lock us down,

00:36:55.910 --> 00:36:59.230
the truth of it is, they've
taken it way too far.

00:36:59.230 --> 00:37:02.340
At the moment, we're
50% locked down still.

00:37:02.340 --> 00:37:04.910
I mean, even though COVID deaths now

00:37:04.910 --> 00:37:07.190
are in single figures every day, right?

00:37:07.190 --> 00:37:09.306
Single figures every day.

00:37:09.306 --> 00:37:14.270
On many days, the number of
road deaths will be bigger

00:37:14.270 --> 00:37:15.920
than the number of COVID deaths.

00:37:15.920 --> 00:37:19.400
And suicides on a lot
of days will be bigger

00:37:19.400 --> 00:37:21.540
than COVID deaths.

00:37:21.540 --> 00:37:24.740
You can go to a pub, but
you can't drink inside.

00:37:24.740 --> 00:37:26.190
You have to drink outside,

00:37:26.190 --> 00:37:28.220
which at this time of the year in England,

00:37:28.220 --> 00:37:29.620
isn't very appealing.

00:37:29.620 --> 00:37:33.000
You can go to a restaurant,
but you can't eat inside,

00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:34.840
you have to eat outside.

00:37:34.840 --> 00:37:37.230
Non-essential shops are back open,

00:37:37.230 --> 00:37:40.210
but the damage that's been
done to them by Amazon

00:37:40.210 --> 00:37:42.070
is just incalculable,

00:37:42.070 --> 00:37:43.720
because that's where we
finished up with this.

00:37:43.720 --> 00:37:45.250
You know, I couldn't go,

00:37:45.250 --> 00:37:47.890
say I wanted to buy a pair
of trainers for my kids.

00:37:47.890 --> 00:37:51.240
I couldn't go to the local
market town and buy them

00:37:51.240 --> 00:37:52.200
because the shop was closed.

00:37:52.200 --> 00:37:54.520
I had to order them through Amazon online.

00:37:54.520 --> 00:37:56.070
And this is one of the great sadnesses.

00:37:56.070 --> 00:37:58.560
It's the little people that have been so,

00:37:58.560 --> 00:38:00.540
it's the self-employed and little people

00:38:00.540 --> 00:38:01.373
that have been hurt.

00:38:01.373 --> 00:38:04.610
And of course, the public
sector, oh, they love it.

00:38:04.610 --> 00:38:05.833
I mean, this is fantastic for them.

00:38:05.833 --> 00:38:08.207
They're being paid to sit
at home and drink beer

00:38:08.207 --> 00:38:10.760
without any threat to their jobs.

00:38:10.760 --> 00:38:13.340
So it's big business and big government

00:38:13.340 --> 00:38:15.170
has benefited from this.

00:38:15.170 --> 00:38:18.870
So look, frankly, we should
have eased up a long time ago.

00:38:18.870 --> 00:38:20.563
But I will say this.

00:38:22.100 --> 00:38:23.880
Boris, despite everything,

00:38:23.880 --> 00:38:25.660
and despite his own personal difficulties,

00:38:25.660 --> 00:38:26.640
of which he's got many.

00:38:26.640 --> 00:38:28.890
I mean, it really is,

00:38:28.890 --> 00:38:31.780
I mean, none of us have
ever lived perfect lives,

00:38:31.780 --> 00:38:36.540
but gosh, his is very, very
complicated to say the least.

00:38:36.540 --> 00:38:39.980
Despite all of that, there's
been one huge success,

00:38:39.980 --> 00:38:41.150
and it's this.

00:38:41.150 --> 00:38:43.230
It's the vaccine rollout, okay?

00:38:43.230 --> 00:38:45.630
So as members of the European Union,

00:38:45.630 --> 00:38:48.600
we were part of the
European Medicines Agency.

00:38:48.600 --> 00:38:50.300
And the European Medicines Agency,

00:38:50.300 --> 00:38:52.610
through an unelected
European commissioner,

00:38:52.610 --> 00:38:55.090
was to make the decision in any pandemic

00:38:55.090 --> 00:38:57.160
as to what should be done.

00:38:57.160 --> 00:39:00.577
We left the European
Medicines Agency with Brexit,

00:39:00.577 --> 00:39:03.310
and The Guardian and others said,

00:39:03.310 --> 00:39:06.310
this proved that Brexit was a death cult,

00:39:06.310 --> 00:39:10.880
because we'd left the all embracing arms

00:39:10.880 --> 00:39:12.280
of this big unelected government.

00:39:12.280 --> 00:39:14.010
And the truth of it is,

00:39:14.010 --> 00:39:17.340
the one thing they have
got spectacularly right,

00:39:17.340 --> 00:39:21.620
they handed this job to a
woman from private equity,

00:39:21.620 --> 00:39:24.780
who in six months, put in place a system,

00:39:24.780 --> 00:39:26.420
as opposed to the EU,

00:39:26.420 --> 00:39:30.360
where a woman from Cyprus
who nobody had ever heard of,

00:39:30.360 --> 00:39:31.893
who nobody ever voted for,

00:39:33.170 --> 00:39:37.190
with a degree in psychology
and no other life achievements

00:39:37.190 --> 00:39:38.530
that I could discern,

00:39:38.530 --> 00:39:41.390
has made an absolute complete
and utter mess of it.

00:39:41.390 --> 00:39:45.020
So you know, basically
we've vaccinated you know,

00:39:45.020 --> 00:39:47.600
three, four, five times
the number of people

00:39:47.600 --> 00:39:48.970
that our European counterparts have,

00:39:48.970 --> 00:39:51.470
and that is being seen as, you know,

00:39:51.470 --> 00:39:53.880
by the way, if you don't
wanna take the vaccine,

00:39:53.880 --> 00:39:56.040
nobody should force you
to take the vaccine,

00:39:56.040 --> 00:40:01.040
but basically, people over
50, people who are overweight,

00:40:01.130 --> 00:40:04.290
people who've got diabetes,
you know, in vast numbers,

00:40:04.290 --> 00:40:06.630
they have gone to get the vaccine,

00:40:06.630 --> 00:40:10.090
and it kind of proves, whether
you're pro-vaccine or not,

00:40:10.090 --> 00:40:12.160
it kind of proves that we're better off

00:40:12.160 --> 00:40:13.690
outside the European Union,

00:40:13.690 --> 00:40:17.390
we're better off making our own decisions.

00:40:17.390 --> 00:40:22.390
And the approval rating
for Brexit is now 70%.

00:40:22.700 --> 00:40:24.220
- I saw that this morning.
- 70%.

00:40:24.220 --> 00:40:25.920
- I mean, that's actually incredible.

00:40:25.920 --> 00:40:30.150
So to you, that must be like
the true reward of this thing

00:40:30.150 --> 00:40:33.350
that when push came to shove,
not only did you get it there,

00:40:33.350 --> 00:40:35.810
but then in the, you
know, year or so since,

00:40:35.810 --> 00:40:36.847
people are actually going,

00:40:36.847 --> 00:40:38.617
"Oh, there was a reason for this,

00:40:38.617 --> 00:40:39.987
"and the country didn't collapse,

00:40:39.987 --> 00:40:41.907
"and racists aren't running in the streets

00:40:41.907 --> 00:40:43.180
"and everything else."

00:40:43.180 --> 00:40:44.510
- Yeah.

00:40:44.510 --> 00:40:47.010
David, I could not be happier.

00:40:47.010 --> 00:40:48.960
You know, how many people,

00:40:48.960 --> 00:40:53.860
how many people set out
with a massive life ambition

00:40:53.860 --> 00:40:55.040
and actually achieve it?

00:40:55.040 --> 00:40:56.110
And I have.

00:40:56.110 --> 00:40:59.410
I mean frankly, I almost
can't believe my luck.

00:40:59.410 --> 00:41:02.311
I mean now.
- It's not luck.

00:41:02.311 --> 00:41:04.220
- Well, there's always a bit of luck.

00:41:04.220 --> 00:41:09.000
But now, I can go to
the local supermarket,

00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:10.910
and walk around and get some shopping

00:41:10.910 --> 00:41:12.630
without a security guard,

00:41:12.630 --> 00:41:13.787
and people are coming up and saying,

00:41:13.787 --> 00:41:14.857
"Well done, Nige.

00:41:14.857 --> 00:41:15.690
"We love it."

00:41:15.690 --> 00:41:17.100
So things have changed a little bit.

00:41:17.100 --> 00:41:19.830
I mean, you know, all
that abuse that I took

00:41:19.830 --> 00:41:21.137
for year, after year, after year,

00:41:21.137 --> 00:41:24.480
you know, the game has changed, we're out.

00:41:24.480 --> 00:41:29.030
In terms of geo politics,
Brexit is the biggest change

00:41:29.030 --> 00:41:31.980
since the fall of the Berlin
Wall over 30 years ago.

00:41:31.980 --> 00:41:35.450
It's the first, you know,
literally the first big kickback

00:41:35.450 --> 00:41:36.960
against globalism,

00:41:36.960 --> 00:41:40.360
and I'm optimistic that other
European countries in time,

00:41:40.360 --> 00:41:41.193
will follow us too.

00:41:41.193 --> 00:41:42.830
- So speaking of other European countries,

00:41:42.830 --> 00:41:45.810
do you sense that some of the
Eastern European countries

00:41:45.810 --> 00:41:47.980
that are doing more on borders right now

00:41:47.980 --> 00:41:49.800
that seem to be fighting

00:41:49.800 --> 00:41:51.740
a lot of the critical race theory stuff,

00:41:51.740 --> 00:41:55.340
not allowing some of the
gender stuff into the system,

00:41:55.340 --> 00:41:58.150
do you sense that they're better
set up to fight this stuff

00:41:58.150 --> 00:42:00.670
than say the UK and America,

00:42:00.670 --> 00:42:04.140
because they were communist
countries and more recently,

00:42:04.140 --> 00:42:06.040
and they sorta get the bad stuff

00:42:06.040 --> 00:42:07.154
that could be on the horizon.

00:42:07.154 --> 00:42:09.090
Is that really why
they're setting up well?

00:42:09.090 --> 00:42:10.737
I'm talking specifically about Poland

00:42:10.737 --> 00:42:12.790
and some of the countries over there.

00:42:12.790 --> 00:42:13.623
- Yeah.

00:42:13.623 --> 00:42:17.026
I mean, have a five minute study

00:42:17.026 --> 00:42:18.960
of the history of Poland
in the 20th century.

00:42:18.960 --> 00:42:21.970
It is a desperate, desperate history.

00:42:21.970 --> 00:42:25.870
You know, I mean, not just
communist, but Nazis invaded,

00:42:25.870 --> 00:42:27.310
I mean, the whole thing.

00:42:27.310 --> 00:42:28.870
So bloody, so awful.

00:42:28.870 --> 00:42:32.230
And of course, the tragedy
in 1945 that, you know,

00:42:32.230 --> 00:42:35.350
as Churchill very much predicted
in that speech at Fulton

00:42:35.350 --> 00:42:38.250
that we finished up with an
Iron Curtain, as he named it,

00:42:38.250 --> 00:42:39.880
down the center of Europe.

00:42:39.880 --> 00:42:41.890
You know, these Poles,

00:42:41.890 --> 00:42:43.940
the reason they joined the European Union

00:42:44.790 --> 00:42:49.070
is because it was sold
in a job lot with NATO.

00:42:49.070 --> 00:42:53.668
Now, if I was a Pole, I would
absolutely want to be in NATO,

00:42:53.668 --> 00:42:55.773
you know, for every reason.

00:42:56.650 --> 00:43:00.920
But now the debate that's going
on in Poland and in Hungary,

00:43:00.920 --> 00:43:05.860
is if unelected bureaucrats
in Brussels are telling us

00:43:05.860 --> 00:43:08.450
who we should appoint to court positions,

00:43:08.450 --> 00:43:11.920
what decisions we should make
on gay marriage or other,

00:43:11.920 --> 00:43:14.420
you know, very important social issues,

00:43:14.420 --> 00:43:16.220
the argument's now resurfacing,

00:43:16.220 --> 00:43:19.080
well hey, what's the
difference between this

00:43:19.080 --> 00:43:21.600
and living under the Soviet Union?

00:43:21.600 --> 00:43:25.040
And you're right about their
culture, their identity,

00:43:25.040 --> 00:43:27.040
and indeed their Christianity.

00:43:27.040 --> 00:43:29.810
Christianity is very, very strong

00:43:29.810 --> 00:43:31.690
in those two countries
that I've mentioned.

00:43:31.690 --> 00:43:35.740
And I think everything
the European Union does

00:43:35.740 --> 00:43:40.560
continues to alienate
those very proud countries.

00:43:40.560 --> 00:43:43.000
And I think at some point, at some point,

00:43:43.000 --> 00:43:45.020
they will not stay part of this Union.

00:43:45.020 --> 00:43:47.270
And the other interesting
dynamic that's going on,

00:43:47.270 --> 00:43:51.660
is the single European
currency, the Euro, all right,

00:43:51.660 --> 00:43:53.960
means that all countries in it

00:43:53.960 --> 00:43:56.520
are in the same economic
and monetary union.

00:43:56.520 --> 00:44:00.840
How can Greece and Germany co-exist

00:44:00.840 --> 00:44:04.750
inside the same economic
amount of treatment?

00:44:04.750 --> 00:44:05.583
They can't.

00:44:05.583 --> 00:44:08.600
It's literally impossible
for cultural reasons.

00:44:08.600 --> 00:44:12.720
And at some point in time, Greece, Italy,

00:44:12.720 --> 00:44:15.200
perhaps even Portugal will decide,

00:44:15.200 --> 00:44:17.520
we simply can't go on like this,

00:44:17.520 --> 00:44:18.840
because you know,

00:44:18.840 --> 00:44:21.640
they've got the wrong
valuation of currency.

00:44:21.640 --> 00:44:22.473
It's hopeless.

00:44:22.473 --> 00:44:25.140
And I remember the late
great Milton Friedman saying,

00:44:25.140 --> 00:44:27.330
that if you get stuck in a currency peg

00:44:27.330 --> 00:44:30.940
that's wrong for your country,
one of two things happens.

00:44:30.940 --> 00:44:34.080
Either you get out and de-value,

00:44:34.080 --> 00:44:37.134
or you de-value the country.

00:44:37.134 --> 00:44:37.967
And you know something--

00:44:37.967 --> 00:44:38.800
- I think Greece knows

00:44:38.800 --> 00:44:39.980
a little something about that right now.

00:44:39.980 --> 00:44:44.980
- Well, since 2009, Greek
GDP is over 25% down.

00:44:47.660 --> 00:44:49.880
And Americans think about that.

00:44:49.880 --> 00:44:52.310
You know, buddy, can you spare us a dime?

00:44:52.310 --> 00:44:54.800
In the Depression, was a 16% fall.

00:44:54.800 --> 00:44:57.550
This is a 25% fall.

00:44:57.550 --> 00:45:01.570
So you know, far from being
this wonderful project

00:45:01.570 --> 00:45:03.860
that was gonna serve all
the peoples of Europe well,

00:45:03.860 --> 00:45:06.530
it's robbing them of their independence,

00:45:06.530 --> 00:45:09.300
it's making huge numbers of them poorer.

00:45:09.300 --> 00:45:12.850
Oh sure, if I was a German
car manufacturer, I'd love it

00:45:12.850 --> 00:45:15.480
because the Deutsche Mark
would be a sight higher

00:45:15.480 --> 00:45:18.920
than the Euro is, so it's been
wonderful for German exports.

00:45:18.920 --> 00:45:23.430
But no, look, I recognized this early on.

00:45:23.430 --> 00:45:27.390
I recognized that this was
just yet another attempt

00:45:27.390 --> 00:45:29.750
to dominate everything
and take everything over.

00:45:29.750 --> 00:45:32.760
I called it in the parliament repeatedly.

00:45:32.760 --> 00:45:34.770
I said, this is the new form of communism.

00:45:34.770 --> 00:45:36.940
And of course, whenever I did that,

00:45:36.940 --> 00:45:40.470
500 of them would start booing,
and screaming, and jeering.

00:45:40.470 --> 00:45:41.893
But hey, it didn't bother me.

00:45:41.893 --> 00:45:43.670
I mean, I rather enjoyed it.

00:45:43.670 --> 00:45:45.970
And that's what it is.

00:45:45.970 --> 00:45:48.150
And of course, for the globalists,

00:45:48.150 --> 00:45:49.600
you know, for people here

00:45:49.600 --> 00:45:51.890
like the Clintons, the Bidens, the Obamas

00:45:51.890 --> 00:45:54.590
who so loved the European Union project,

00:45:54.590 --> 00:45:58.530
Brussels is the epicenter
of the globalist project.

00:45:58.530 --> 00:46:02.260
And if we can defeat that,
I really genuinely believe

00:46:02.260 --> 00:46:04.830
we're taking the free world,
or putting the free world back

00:46:04.830 --> 00:46:05.740
into a far better place.

00:46:05.740 --> 00:46:07.930
- Who do you think is
behind the Biden thing?

00:46:07.930 --> 00:46:09.660
I mean well, do you think it's Biden

00:46:09.660 --> 00:46:10.890
that's behind the Biden thing?

00:46:10.890 --> 00:46:12.380
That seems to be the question people say,

00:46:12.380 --> 00:46:14.400
okay, is it the Clinton machine behind it?

00:46:14.400 --> 00:46:15.570
Is it the Obama machine?

00:46:15.570 --> 00:46:16.480
Is there a distinction?

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:17.520
But like, who do you think

00:46:17.520 --> 00:46:20.563
is really kind of driving this thing?

00:46:21.830 --> 00:46:22.990
- Well it can't be him obviously.

00:46:22.990 --> 00:46:25.360
I mean, you know, look, he's
just a duffer, isn't he?

00:46:25.360 --> 00:46:28.180
I mean, he can barely
string a sentence together.

00:46:28.180 --> 00:46:30.690
And so he's quite malleable.

00:46:30.690 --> 00:46:33.580
And for some of those
with a hard left agenda,

00:46:33.580 --> 00:46:35.340
that makes him quite useful

00:46:35.340 --> 00:46:37.070
because he isn't gonna resist too much.

00:46:37.070 --> 00:46:40.587
I'm also told that his actual work rate,

00:46:40.587 --> 00:46:41.570
and it's down to just

00:46:41.570 --> 00:46:43.680
less than a handful of hours every day.

00:46:43.680 --> 00:46:45.907
He's just physically not up to it.

00:46:45.907 --> 00:46:48.590
And I've been asking him the
same question that you've asked

00:46:48.590 --> 00:46:50.010
in the last two weeks here.

00:46:50.010 --> 00:46:53.060
The common consensus is that Team Obama

00:46:53.060 --> 00:46:55.698
still have a massive hand
to play in all of this.

00:46:55.698 --> 00:46:58.740
And I don't know enough, maybe you do.

00:46:58.740 --> 00:47:00.660
I don't know enough to contradict this,

00:47:00.660 --> 00:47:03.660
but that certainly from
those who I would judge

00:47:03.660 --> 00:47:05.100
to be in the know, that's the argument.

00:47:05.100 --> 00:47:07.120
- You remember there was that
famous interview years ago

00:47:07.120 --> 00:47:08.600
where Obama said it would be great

00:47:08.600 --> 00:47:10.320
if he could just not be President,

00:47:10.320 --> 00:47:11.990
but be pulling the strings from behind.

00:47:11.990 --> 00:47:15.010
That would be pretty, I mean,
the guy said it himself.

00:47:15.010 --> 00:47:15.843
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:47:15.843 --> 00:47:16.940
Well, I think to some degree,

00:47:16.940 --> 00:47:18.060
that does appear to be happening, yeah.

00:47:18.060 --> 00:47:19.810
- Do you sense now that
you're here in America,

00:47:19.810 --> 00:47:22.320
and you're on tour and you're
in the middle of the country,

00:47:22.320 --> 00:47:23.533
and seeing the heartland and everything,

00:47:23.533 --> 00:47:27.740
that America is uniquely
set up to fight this,

00:47:27.740 --> 00:47:29.990
even though maybe we
can't see it right now,

00:47:29.990 --> 00:47:33.190
but our history, the
way we left King George,

00:47:33.190 --> 00:47:36.720
the way we fought for
independence in a very unique way,

00:47:36.720 --> 00:47:38.180
the way that this country was set up

00:47:38.180 --> 00:47:40.940
as an idea for all people.

00:47:40.940 --> 00:47:43.830
Is that in essence the thing
that you really wanna reignite,

00:47:43.830 --> 00:47:46.300
and is that why you've got
that flag behind you right now?

00:47:46.300 --> 00:47:47.390
- Yes.

00:47:47.390 --> 00:47:51.000
Yes, yeah, you know, I
mean I'm not American,

00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:53.580
but I have a huge, as I've
said already in this interview,

00:47:53.580 --> 00:47:55.000
a huge self-interest,

00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:58.030
and I care passionately what
happens in this country.

00:47:58.030 --> 00:47:59.730
And you're right, you know,

00:47:59.730 --> 00:48:03.340
when American children were
being taught properly at school,

00:48:03.340 --> 00:48:05.370
I'm not sure they all are these days,

00:48:05.370 --> 00:48:08.390
but they were being taught
all about the revolution,

00:48:08.390 --> 00:48:12.020
breaking free, about liberty,
about the amazing constitution

00:48:12.020 --> 00:48:14.690
that those brilliant minds put together.

00:48:14.690 --> 00:48:16.840
So yeah, I think it is deeply ingrained

00:48:16.840 --> 00:48:18.730
within the American people.

00:48:18.730 --> 00:48:22.210
Of course, you know through
welfarism and other problems,

00:48:22.210 --> 00:48:25.010
you know, there is a growth
of the leftist ideology,

00:48:25.010 --> 00:48:29.240
but it is still a small activist minority.

00:48:29.240 --> 00:48:32.270
And what you've gotta do is to reach out.

00:48:32.270 --> 00:48:35.477
You know, there's something like 30, 40%,

00:48:35.477 --> 00:48:38.640
40% who just don't vote
in American elections.

00:48:38.640 --> 00:48:41.650
And yet their lives are
being directly affected

00:48:41.650 --> 00:48:42.820
by what has happened.

00:48:42.820 --> 00:48:44.560
We got Brexit.

00:48:44.560 --> 00:48:47.010
We got Brexit, we won that referendum

00:48:47.010 --> 00:48:48.970
because two and a half million people

00:48:48.970 --> 00:48:51.730
who literally never voted
in their lives came out

00:48:51.730 --> 00:48:53.710
because they believed they
can make a difference.

00:48:53.710 --> 00:48:56.450
And I think if the Republican candidates

00:48:56.450 --> 00:48:58.000
can get that message out,

00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:00.260
and it's not just the negative message,

00:49:00.260 --> 00:49:02.350
but it is genuinely about how

00:49:02.350 --> 00:49:04.080
they could make life better for people.

00:49:04.080 --> 00:49:06.820
You've gotta mobilize those
that don't normally vote.

00:49:06.820 --> 00:49:09.790
And I think America's history
does lend itself to that,

00:49:09.790 --> 00:49:10.623
yes, I do.

00:49:10.623 --> 00:49:12.290
- Yeah, can you, we're
gonna link obviously

00:49:12.290 --> 00:49:13.320
to the tour down below,

00:49:13.320 --> 00:49:14.460
but what are you doing?

00:49:14.460 --> 00:49:16.110
What are you actually doing on the tour?

00:49:16.110 --> 00:49:17.770
I mean, are you just giving speeches?

00:49:17.770 --> 00:49:19.590
Are you going up with other politicians?

00:49:19.590 --> 00:49:20.623
What are you doing?

00:49:21.830 --> 00:49:25.680
- No, I'm basically
going to activist groups.

00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:27.470
And in some towns we go through,

00:49:27.470 --> 00:49:29.960
that might be 30 people meeting in a bar.

00:49:29.960 --> 00:49:33.650
At other events, you know, I'm
speaking at events in Arizona

00:49:33.650 --> 00:49:36.630
where, that's in a couple of
weeks time, where, you know,

00:49:36.630 --> 00:49:38.010
500 have booked tickets already,

00:49:38.010 --> 00:49:39.460
and I've no doubt it'll
be a lot bigger than that

00:49:39.460 --> 00:49:40.293
on the day.

00:49:40.293 --> 00:49:43.550
But I am meeting the people
who give of their time,

00:49:43.550 --> 00:49:46.447
their love, their energy,
people that really care,

00:49:46.447 --> 00:49:49.180
and I'm going out and meeting
them in their thousands

00:49:49.180 --> 00:49:52.090
and trying to re-motivate them,

00:49:52.090 --> 00:49:53.180
trying to get them out of.

00:49:53.180 --> 00:49:57.470
And when I sit and talk to
them, they are very, very down.

00:49:57.470 --> 00:49:58.710
Very, very down indeed.

00:49:58.710 --> 00:50:01.730
So I'm trying through the Brexit example,

00:50:01.730 --> 00:50:03.420
and also the immigration issue,

00:50:03.420 --> 00:50:05.160
to explain to them that you know,

00:50:05.160 --> 00:50:08.020
a huge victory may not be too far away.

00:50:08.020 --> 00:50:09.300
So that's the main emphasis.

00:50:09.300 --> 00:50:12.070
Obviously I'm doing media,
various other things like that.

00:50:12.070 --> 00:50:15.460
But really, this is about
getting out with freedom works

00:50:15.460 --> 00:50:19.280
and meeting these people
who did such a great job.

00:50:19.280 --> 00:50:20.880
I mean, just look at the House,

00:50:20.880 --> 00:50:22.680
you know, where the party picked up seats.

00:50:22.680 --> 00:50:25.437
And you know, I've met
Congressmen and women who say,

00:50:25.437 --> 00:50:26.737
"Look, we love this organization

00:50:26.737 --> 00:50:29.657
"because when we need help, when we shout,

00:50:29.657 --> 00:50:31.680
"people, keen people arrive."

00:50:31.680 --> 00:50:36.290
So it is about motivation,
and it's also too,

00:50:36.290 --> 00:50:39.680
I want to raise an issue which is,

00:50:39.680 --> 00:50:41.730
most people in and around politics,

00:50:41.730 --> 00:50:44.827
they think that the grassroots
bit doesn't really matter.

00:50:44.827 --> 00:50:47.360
And it's the least
glamorous bit of politics.

00:50:47.360 --> 00:50:50.570
But I know from all the races
that I've been involved in,

00:50:50.570 --> 00:50:53.590
and particularly when we
got Brexit back on track,

00:50:53.590 --> 00:50:57.350
I know that a good grassroots
campaign is the absolute key,

00:50:57.350 --> 00:50:59.160
because remember this,

00:50:59.160 --> 00:51:01.590
on the left side of the
debate here in America,

00:51:01.590 --> 00:51:03.130
you've got the trade unions,

00:51:03.130 --> 00:51:04.490
you've got many of the students,

00:51:04.490 --> 00:51:07.140
they have an army on the ground.

00:51:07.140 --> 00:51:10.620
And at the moment, I don't
believe the Republican Party

00:51:10.620 --> 00:51:14.960
does have one of sufficient
scale and sufficient size.

00:51:14.960 --> 00:51:18.640
So I'm trying to push that
argument that everybody can help.

00:51:18.640 --> 00:51:21.910
It's no good just turning
up and clapping somebody.

00:51:21.910 --> 00:51:23.960
You've actually, if you believe in this,

00:51:23.960 --> 00:51:25.897
you've gotta commit that
you're gonna do something.

00:51:25.897 --> 00:51:29.370
And it doesn't matter if you're 97

00:51:29.370 --> 00:51:31.870
and sitting in a wheelchair,
you can still do something.

00:51:31.870 --> 00:51:33.360
You can still make some phone calls.

00:51:33.360 --> 00:51:35.750
There are still things
that everybody can do.

00:51:35.750 --> 00:51:39.820
And if you really do
want to save your country

00:51:39.820 --> 00:51:41.520
from hard left socialism,

00:51:41.520 --> 00:51:44.480
sitting around and
complaining isn't the answer.

00:51:44.480 --> 00:51:46.530
Positive attitude, energy, and action is.

00:51:46.530 --> 00:51:48.520
- Do you think it's kind
of funny that you ended up,

00:51:48.520 --> 00:51:51.190
you did the Brexit thing, and
now you're here doing this,

00:51:51.190 --> 00:51:53.770
and it's like, there'll
probably be something else

00:51:53.770 --> 00:51:55.340
that you'll be fighting for in 10 years.

00:51:55.340 --> 00:51:57.990
You don't strike me as
someone that will ever retire.

00:51:58.849 --> 00:52:02.563
- I wouldn't have thought
so for a moment, no, no.

00:52:02.563 --> 00:52:06.220
I mean, I like campaigning,
and at the end of the day,

00:52:06.220 --> 00:52:07.760
I think the most important thing

00:52:07.760 --> 00:52:09.550
we can all do as human beings,

00:52:09.550 --> 00:52:11.800
and as early as possible if we can,

00:52:11.800 --> 00:52:13.760
find out what you're good at.

00:52:13.760 --> 00:52:16.090
Find out the one thing in
life that you're good at

00:52:16.090 --> 00:52:16.923
and pursue it.

00:52:16.923 --> 00:52:18.020
And I'll be honest with you,

00:52:18.020 --> 00:52:19.910
there are lots of things I'm terrible at,

00:52:19.910 --> 00:52:21.820
lots of things I'm hopeless at.

00:52:21.820 --> 00:52:25.060
But I've always, I like people,

00:52:25.060 --> 00:52:27.130
I'm very gregarious, I'm very social,

00:52:27.130 --> 00:52:29.357
as you mentioned earlier
on in the chat we've had,

00:52:29.357 --> 00:52:31.190
and I love going out.

00:52:31.190 --> 00:52:34.167
I love going out,
meeting groups of people.

00:52:34.167 --> 00:52:36.220
And I think I can do my little bit,

00:52:36.220 --> 00:52:38.780
perhaps to spread a
little bit of inspiration,

00:52:38.780 --> 00:52:39.800
a little bit of optimism.

00:52:39.800 --> 00:52:41.410
So no, I'm gonna go on fighting

00:52:41.410 --> 00:52:42.970
for these Conservative causes

00:52:42.970 --> 00:52:44.850
across the English speaking world.

00:52:44.850 --> 00:52:47.680
And so I'll do stuff in
the UK, I'll do stuff here.

00:52:47.680 --> 00:52:49.650
I can't wait to get back to Australia

00:52:49.650 --> 00:52:51.840
to do more stuff down there.

00:52:51.840 --> 00:52:54.163
As for New Zealand, I'm not
quite sure where we stand there,

00:52:54.163 --> 00:52:57.180
given that they've now
basically sold their souls

00:52:57.180 --> 00:52:58.660
to the Chinese Communist Party,

00:52:58.660 --> 00:52:59.880
which should be a warning to all of us.

00:52:59.880 --> 00:53:03.330
So no, I love this, I love
campaigning, I love life,

00:53:03.330 --> 00:53:05.810
and yeah, I'm gonna keep on running.

00:53:05.810 --> 00:53:07.630
- Well Nigel, I love this interview.

00:53:07.630 --> 00:53:10.570
So I hope I can join you
on tour at some point

00:53:10.570 --> 00:53:11.420
in the midst of this thing.

00:53:11.420 --> 00:53:13.280
We're trying to coordinate
a couple of things,

00:53:13.280 --> 00:53:14.840
but I think the message
that you're bringing

00:53:14.840 --> 00:53:17.610
is exactly what Americans
need to hear right now.

00:53:17.610 --> 00:53:19.370
It's kind of funny that it's coming

00:53:19.370 --> 00:53:20.870
from somebody from the UK,

00:53:20.870 --> 00:53:22.740
but we'll take it in this strange time,

00:53:22.740 --> 00:53:24.870
so I wish you luck with everything.

00:53:24.870 --> 00:53:25.703
- Well, thank you.

00:53:25.703 --> 00:53:28.120
And remember this, culturally,

00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:31.160
the UK and America have
never ever been closer.

00:53:31.160 --> 00:53:33.670
You know, my kids watch
American television,

00:53:33.670 --> 00:53:34.930
taxi drivers here talk to me

00:53:34.930 --> 00:53:37.560
about Downton Abbey or The Crown.

00:53:37.560 --> 00:53:39.880
NFL is now very popular in England.

00:53:39.880 --> 00:53:42.850
Soccer's becoming popular here in the USA.

00:53:42.850 --> 00:53:44.510
And just a final thought on this,

00:53:44.510 --> 00:53:45.910
when Donald Trump was on tour,

00:53:45.910 --> 00:53:47.900
you know, make America great again,

00:53:47.900 --> 00:53:51.180
emphasizing those three
words, "Made in the USA".

00:53:51.180 --> 00:53:52.820
Everything had to be American.

00:53:52.820 --> 00:53:55.470
And as Air Force One
appeared on the horizon,

00:53:55.470 --> 00:53:56.900
and the music started to play,

00:53:56.900 --> 00:53:59.250
there was such a big feature
of the Trump rallies,

00:53:59.250 --> 00:54:00.570
what music did we get?

00:54:00.570 --> 00:54:03.850
Well, we got David Bowie, and
Elton John, and Phil Collins.

00:54:03.850 --> 00:54:06.400
And actually, it's difficult
with popular music now to tell

00:54:06.400 --> 00:54:09.040
whether it's British, or
whether it's American.

00:54:09.040 --> 00:54:13.020
So perhaps a Brit coming
here, giving this message,

00:54:13.020 --> 00:54:15.970
is not quite as strange as
people might first think.

00:54:15.970 --> 00:54:17.020
- We'll take it, we'll take it.

00:54:17.020 --> 00:54:18.760
Nigel Farage, thank you so much.

00:54:18.760 --> 00:54:20.620
And we're gonna link to
everything right down below.

